                        "review": "A good video game should feel like a playground and that's how this game feels. I find myself playing instead of grinding for points or slogging through exposition to get to the next plot point.\r\n\r\nThe main game feels like a playground, where I get to skate around on rocket skates, float in the water on an innertube, or sneak around and hide from the enemies. There's also rhythm minigames and an obstacle course minigame.\r\n\r\nThe vibe of this game is superb. Fantastic music, wonderful animations, and cartoonish characters. There's no grand drama about saving the world or self-discovery. Just a couple friends trying to have a good time while they get themselves out of the trouble they got into.",
